  "takeaways": [
    "Lost spells were mostly short possessions: 36% of true spells last under 3 s and V10 found 1% (<1 s) and 8-10% (1-3 s).",
    "V12 turnover model: +0.090 to +0.130 over V10 on the bench; 1-3 s spells found 24-32%, 3-10 s 60-70%. Not yet run on BAR-ATH.",
    "V11 formation dead ball: +0.027 to +0.033 over V10 on the bench, but labels 49% of BAR-ATH as dead (V2: 19%); not adopted.",
    "V10 gap model: beats V9 at 25-40% hidden ball; transfers to BAR-ATH at 84% agreement with clear control; public 0.4114.",
    "Dead ball explains few lost spells on the bench (27 of 1,145 merges); turnovers explain most."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Event-derived Metrica labels may differ from BAR-ATH corrected-tracking labels; V12 may partly learn Metrica labelling style.",
    "Simulated live-ball gaps, one random draw per level; Metrica dead ball is easier than BAR-ATH.",
    "BAR-ATH public scores reuse 17 inspected spells and contain 35 s of long gaps.",
    "All methods are offline and use frames after the current one."
  ]
}
